            "short_desc": "Profiles data quality for specified fields in a batch of records",
            "desc": "Computes a data quality profile for each specified field: missing rates, "
                "type distribution, value ranges, cardinality, and outlier detection. Use this "
                "to understand your data before building models or to monitor data quality in "
                "production pipelines.\n\n"
                "**What you get per field**:\n"
                "- `missing_rate` — fraction of records with null/missing values\n"
                "- `type` — most common Qore type seen (string, int, float, etc.)\n"
                "- `cardinality` — number of unique values\n"
                "- For numeric fields: `min`, `max`, `mean`, `std` (standard deviation)\n"
                "- `outlier_count` — values beyond 1.5*IQR from Q1/Q3 (numeric fields with "
                ">= 10 values)\n\n"
                "Records accumulate in a batch; when full, one profile event per field is "
                "emitted.",
            "action_code": DPAT_PIPELINE_PROCESSOR,
            "processor_capabilities": DPC_AGGREGATE,
            "cls": "DataProviderML::QoreDataProfileProcessor",
            "groups": ("Data Governance",),
            "options": DataProviderActionCatalog::getActionOptionFromFields(
                QoreDataProfileProcessor::ConstructorOptions{"fields", "window_size"}, {
                    "preselected": True,
                    "required": True,
                    "loc": "constructor",
